+# Decisions Register
+
+Status: living register  
+Owner role: Product owner (entries for architecture decisions: tech lead)  
+Last updated: 2026-09-30
+
+Append new decisions at the end with the next ID. Never delete an entry; mark it `superseded by D-xxx`. An architecture decision that needs more than a few lines gets its own file in `docs/adr/` and a row here.
+
+Status values: `decided` (the owner approved it), `assumption` (a working choice that the owner must confirm; see `docs/open-items.md`), `superseded`.
+
+| ID | Date | Decision | Why | Source | Status |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| D-001 | 2026-09-30 | V4 documents (now 01, 03, 05, 07 in `docs/spec/`) are the product authority. 02-DETAILED-SPECIFICATION supplies implementation detail where V4 is silent. On conflict, V4 wins unless a decision in this register says otherwise. | V4 has the broader scope and governance; the detailed spec has the build-level detail. | Owner review, 30 Sep 2026; 09-MERGE-DECISIONS | decided |
+| D-002 | 2026-09-30 | Anonymous reports are an interactive in-app web report only. No PDF, document, CSV, JSON, evidence or task download for anonymous users, denied server-side. Private unguessable link plus signed access secret, noindex, deletable any time, expires after 7 days at most. No email gate. | Privacy and cost; owner chose the V4 rule over the earlier 30-day, PDF-allowed brief. | Owner answer, 30 Sep 2026 | decided |
+| D-003 | 2026-09-30 | Registered-project evidence retention defaults to 30 days unless an approved plan or policy says otherwise. | Carried from V4 §9. | 01 §9 | decided |
+| D-004 | 2026-09-30 | Identity starts as `User → Project → Site`. Organizations, agency workspaces, invitations and advanced roles arrive at M11. Claiming an anonymous audit never proves domain ownership. | Simplest model that supports the first milestones. | 01 §5.0; 05 §1.1 | decided |
+| D-005 | 2026-09-30 | One hard monthly cap of USD 150 covers Google Cloud hosting and infrastructure plus AI-model and data-provider calls. The cost guard tracks hosting and paid calls as separate lines against the one cap. | Owner answered "1 and 2" to the budget-scope question; read conservatively as one combined cap. | Owner answer, 30 Sep 2026 | assumption (confirm) |
+| D-006 | 2026-09-30 | Crawl sizes, prompt-panel sizes and anonymous tier scopes are configuration, not constants. Defaults (ASSUMPTION): rich anonymous audit up to 20 representative pages; free AI panel 8 prompts x configured providers x 1 run, shown as counts; connected panel 20-40 prompts x 3 runs. | V4 rejected fixed universal sizes. | 01 §15; `config/anonymous-eligibility.yaml`; `config/prompt-panels/` | decided (defaults are assumptions) |
+| D-007 | 2026-09-30 | Per-audit paid-call caps: soft USD 3.00, hard USD 4.00. Circuit breaker opens after 3 consecutive timeouts or 5xx errors, 15-minute cool-down, one probe. | Carried from the detailed spec until the M0B cost proof measures real costs. | 02 §18; `config/budgets.yaml` | assumption |
+| D-008 | 2026-09-30 | Stack: strict TypeScript, Next.js on Cloud Run, Cloud Run Jobs for crawl and render, Cloud Tasks, Pub/Sub, Workflows, Cloud SQL for PostgreSQL, Cloud Storage, Secret Manager, KMS, Cloud Armor, Terraform. Package manager pnpm (ASSUMPTION, confirm at M0A). Identity Platform is the candidate identity provider, not yet decided (see D-011). | Carried from V4 §10 and the detailed spec §12. | 01 §10; 02 §12 | decided (pnpm and identity provider open) |
+| D-009 | 2026-09-30 | Only the product's sandboxed crawler fetches in production. The vendored skill's scripts are reference implementations and golden-file generators only. No Google Autocomplete and no search-result scraping in the product. | Safety, terms of service and reproducibility. | 09-MERGE-DECISIONS (V4 "Rejected"); 02 §13 | decided |
+| D-010 | 2026-09-30 | No hard-coded model IDs, prices, quotas or crawler tokens. They live in `config/` with a source, checked date and owner. | Platform facts change. | 03 "Required configuration" | decided |
+| D-011 | 2026-09-30 | Open until M0: Google Cloud organization and region, identity provider, first CMS or Git connector, runtime AI providers and the data classes each may receive. Placeholders `<DECIDE_AT_M0: ...>` mark them. | Owner decisions. | 01 §14; 05 §9 | open |
+| D-012 | 2026-09-30 | Product name Website Presence Intelligence (WPI). Scores: Presence Readiness (deterministic, 0-100, 7 categories) and Experience Effectiveness (reviewed, separate). Neither is ever blended with the other, with observed AI visibility or with search performance. | V4 product model. | 01 §5.2, §5.3 | decided |
+| D-013 | 2026-09-30 | BigQuery holds the Cloud Billing export and the cost-ledger reconciliation. | The cost guard needs the Billing export (D-005); the detailed spec already names BigQuery for the ledger. | 02 §12, §18; `config/budgets.yaml` | assumption (confirm at M0B) |
+| D-014 | 2026-09-30 | Until M11, every record is owned by a project, directly through `project_id` (and `site_id` where relevant) or through its parent record (for example an Approval through its ChangeSet), and every query filters by project. M0B writes the parent-join rule for every schema without `project_id` (OI-040). `organization_id` arrives with agency tenancy at M11. | Follows D-004; replaces the detailed spec's early `tenant_id`/`workspace_id`. | 03; `schemas/` | decided |
+| D-015 | 2026-09-30 | Canonical vocabulary: plan groups `critical_blocker`, `quick_win`, `strategic_opportunity`, `measurement_fix`, `polish`; evidence states `verified`, `inferred`, `client_stated`, `estimated`, `not_verified`, `unavailable` with the fidelity-label mapping in 03. | Resolves differences between V4 and the detailed spec. | 03; `schemas/common.schema.json` | decided |
+| D-016 | 2026-09-30 | Automatic rollback only under V4's four conditions (01 §15); otherwise pause for human review. MCP servers are build and calibration tools unless production-approved with equivalent auth, scopes, tenancy, logging and tests. | V4 rules are stricter than the detailed spec's earlier text. | 01 §15 | decided |
+| D-017 | 2026-09-30 | Pull-request checks run in GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`); image build and promotion use Cloud Build and Cloud Deploy. | Keeps merge gates in the repository host and deployment inside Google Cloud. | 02 §12; 05 §12 | assumption (confirm at M0A) |
+| D-018 | 2026-09-30 | Claude Code model assignments follow 06-MODEL-PLAN: `fable` for M0B, M1, M9, M11, M13 and security-critical slices; `opus` for M2, M6, M8B, M12; `opusplan` otherwise. The project default is `opusplan` in plan mode. | Match model capability to risk. | 06-MODEL-PLAN | decided (recheck model availability at M0A) |
